## Your job

- `src/agent/prompt.md` - the system prompt
- `agent.yaml` - `uses_mcp` lists the MCP servers; tools come from them at run time
- `evals/dataset.jsonl` - real questions with expected answers (`expect_contains`, `expect_absent`, `expect_tool`)
- More nodes in `src/agent/graph.py` only when you need them. Identity code (`auth.py`, `gateway.py`) is the template's.

## Run it on a laptop

Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
py -3.11 -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -e <i2-platform-auth folder>     # a PATH - never `pip install platform-auth` (different package on PyPI)
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
Copy-Item .env.example .env.local                     # fill it in; never commit it
python -m pytest -q tests
python -m dotenv -f .env.local run -- langgraph dev --port 2024 --no-browser
python run_agent_test.py "your question"
```

macOS / Linux: the same with `python3.11 -m venv .venv`, `. .venv/bin/activate`, `cp .env.example .env.local`.

## MCP route

`MCP_ROUTE=direct` calls each server at `MCP_URL_<SERVER>` (migration). `MCP_ROUTE=gateway` calls
`{GATEWAY_URL}/mcp/<server>/mcp` (APIM) with an On-Behalf-Of token per server and needs `agent_auth=entra`.
Switching to entra later: `copier update -a .copier-answers.yml --data agent_auth=entra` (or regenerate).

## Build and deploy

```bash
pip wheel --no-deps -w vendor <i2-platform-auth folder>   # once per platform-auth version
langgraph build -t <acr>.azurecr.us/{{ name }}:<tag>
docker push <acr>.azurecr.us/{{ name }}:<tag>
```

Then point the LangSmith deployment at the new image. Company CA certificates: see `certs/README.md`.
